    "description": "The 2026 Academy Awards featured the seventh tie in the Oscars' history, with two live-action short films, 'The Singers' and 'Two People Exchanging Saliva,' winning the best live-action short category."
    "articleSummary": "The Oscars on March 15, 2026, saw the seventh tie in the awards show's history, occurring in the best live-action short film category. The two short films, 'The Singers' and 'Two People Exchanging Saliva,' were awarded the title. Although hosts Kumail Nanjiani and Conan O'Brien joked about the long delay, the filmmakers from both categories competed to deliver speeches. The event followed a 1995 tie in the same category and a 2013 tie in sound editing. While previous ties sometimes involved votes within a margin, the 2026 tie was directly for the award, with both films officially recognized as winners. Previous Oscar ties had occurred in 'best actor' (1969), 'best actress' (1932), 'best documentary short' (1950), 'best documentary' (1987), 'best sound editing' (2013), 'best actor' (1932), 'best director' (1987), and 'best supporting actress' (1987)."
    "points": [
        "The 2026 Oscars featured a tie in the best live-action short film category.",
