    "articleSummary": "The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention updated its global polio travel advisory with a Level 2 (second‑lowest) status, adding more than two dozen nations—including Laos and Namibia—to the list while removing Finland, Ghana, Spain, and Zimbabwe. The advisory reflects detection of poliovirus in humans or environmental samples within the past 13 months. It recommends that travelers be up to date on vaccinations and that adults who have completed their routine series consider a booster dose. The CDC also reminds the public that polio is a highly contagious infection capable of causing paralysis in rare cases, with symptoms such as fever, headache, nausea, and nerve pain, and that treatment focuses on symptom management rather than curing the virus.",
