    "articleSummary": "In two separate appearances in March 2026, President Donald Trump asserted that an unnamed former president confessed regret for not launching an attack on Iran, which he characterized as something only he had done. He described these conversations as private discussions he wished he could repeat, claiming no other president had shown the courage to act. Trump claimed the former president said, 'I wish I did it, I wish I did,' implying a silent opportunity that Trump was finally embracing. Trump has also been highly critical of both President Joe Biden and former President Barack Obama, whom he accuses of unfavorable Iran-related deals. Meanwhile, all four living former presidents—Bill Clinton, George W. Bush, Barack Obama, and Joe Biden—have publicly confirmed they have not spoken to Trump since 2025, and the White House has not acknowledged any such private conversations.",
