    "The four living former presidents said they have not been in touch with Trump recently.",
    "Trump said he does not want to name the former president to avoid embarrassment."
  ],
  "biasSummary": "The article appears to support Trump’s narrative of moral leadership while downplaying verification, presenting his claim with confidence and his denial of former presidents’ contact with a skeptical tone. This perspective is largely aligned with a right‑leaning media view that favors Trump’s self‑portrayal as the only president willing to confront Iran."
}

{
    "description": "Donald Trump's controversial commentary on the US involvement in the war in Iran, questioning the necessity of securing the Strait of Hormuz and criticizing allies for not providing military support.",
    "articleSummary": "Donald Trump drew backlash for suggesting that the US military operation in Iran to secure the Strait of Hormuz was unnecessary, asking if they shouldn’t even be there given the country’s significant oil reserves. The president, speaking to reporters on Air Force One, demanded that European and NATO allies assist in the effort, which has already begun, instead of questioning the war itself. His comments followed criticism that he failed to clearly state the reasons for the conflict. The US faces ongoing pressure from allies like Australia, France, Japan, and the UK to join efforts to reopen the strait, which is critical to global oil supplies. Trump has reversed prior positions on outside assistance, is consulting with multiple countries—including China, though unlikely due to its close ties with Iran—about military support, and has vowed to delay a China summit if allies fail to act. His remarks underscore a broader tension between US strategic interests in the region and the growing reluctance of allies to take sides in the war.",
